    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `checkDigit` as a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` integer field (0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains `getCheckDigit`/`setCheckDigit`.\n\n2. **`CustomerCodeCheckDigit.java`** (new helper in the owner function package) \u2014 computes the standard Luhn check digit over just the digit characters in the customer code, ignoring the `-` separators and letter prefixes. It mirrors the algorithm the acceptance test uses (`(10 - sum % 10) % 10`, doubling every second digit from the right).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that populates `checkDigit` from `CustomerCodeCheckDigit.of(owner.getCustomerCode())`, matching the existing pattern for other derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `identityKey`, etc.).\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` test \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts it equals the returned `checkDigit` \u2014 passes.",
